BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ars-electronica-u19-create-your-world-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270303
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270304
SUMMARY:Deadline: Prix Ars Electronica: u19 create your world 2027 (Austria
 \, under 20)
DESCRIPTION:u19 create your world is the youth category of the Prix Ars Ele
 ctronica\, for young people in Austria working with digital media\, techno
 logy\, games\, code\, film\, music\, art and design. Individuals\, project
  groups and school projects may enter. There are two categories: Young Cre
 atives (up to 14\, judged in u10\, u12 and u14 age groups) and Young Profe
 ssionals (14 to 19)\, whose Golden Nica carries EUR 3\,000. ELIGIBILITY: e
 ntrants must be no older than 19 and live in Austria at the submission dea
 dline. Submissions are open now through the online database at calls.ars.e
 lectronica.art/2027/u19/ until 3 March 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Ars Electron
 ica (Prix Ars Electronica)\nLocation: Linz\, Austria\; open only to people
  aged 19 or younger who live in Austria on 3 March 2027\nAward: Young Prof
 essionals (14 to 19): Golden Nica EUR 3\,000\, two Awards of Distinction E
 UR 800 each\, ten Honorary Mentions. Young Creatives (up to 14): per age g
 roup (u10\, u12\, u14) one EUR 500 Prize plus an Award of Distinction (EUR
  150 for u14\, EUR 100 for u12 and u10). No entry fee mentioned.\nDuration
 : One-off prize\n\nMore: https://ars.electronica.art/createyourworld/en/pr
 ix/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ars.electronica.art/createyourworld/en/prix/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Linz\, Austria\; open only to people aged 19 or younger who live i
 n Austria on 3 March 2027
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-horizons-parma-360-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Horizons: Art Beyond Algorithms (PARMA 360 Festival\, 
 Parma European Youth Capital 2027)
DESCRIPTION:First edition of an international call for artists under 35 wor
 king with artificial intelligence\, digital languages and emerging technol
 ogies\, run by 360° Creativity Events APS for PARMA 360 Festival and Parm
 a European Youth Capital 2027. It follows the 2026 pilot exhibition SYNTHE
 TIC HORIZONS (curated by Chiara Canali). The call focuses on open-source a
 nd closed-source image and video generation tools and their creative\, soc
 ial and cultural impact. THEMES: Parma Heritage (crafts\, traditions\, arc
 hives\, immersive storytelling of the city)\; La Cura / Care (wellbeing\, 
 accessibility\, AI ethics\, health tech\, public space)\; Sustainability a
 nd Data Ecology (energy and water cost of AI\, data extraction and digital
  colonialism\, waste of digital images\, ethics of automated production). 
 ACCEPTED FORMATS: digital and synthetic images\, NFTs\, printed digital ph
 otography\, digital/3D-printed sculpture\, video\, audio\, interactive bro
 wser or chatbot installations\, software art\, VR\, AR\, sound art\, perfo
 rmance and hybrids. Works must already be completed but need not be unpubl
 ished. One application per artist. REQUIRED: an Artist Statement (max 1\,5
 00 characters) on how you use AI\, naming software\, models and workflow\;
  missing statements are excluded. SELECTION: a jury of the PARMA 360 artis
 tic direction\, the Parma EYC27 committee and AI/new-tech experts picks 20
  finalists (at least 3 from the Parma area)\, announced from 1 December 20
 26\; finalists show in a group exhibition curated by Chiara Canali in Parm
 a in April-May 2027. The organiser covers shipping to the show and AV equi
 pment hire and gives finalists one hotel night at the opening\; return shi
 pping and travel are at the artist's cost. Prize-winning works are acquire
 d in full or in part. AGE: must not have turned 35 by the closing date. DE
 ADLINE: 31 October 2026\, midnight Rome time\, via the Google Form linked 
 in the call. Questions: aihorizonscall@gmail.com.\n\nOrganisation: 360° C
 reativity Events APS (PARMA 360 Festival della creatività contemporanea)\
 , with Parma European Youth Capital 2027\nLocation: Parma\, Italy. Open to
  Italian and international artists under 35 and students of the Accademie 
 di Belle Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in April-May 2027.\nAward: EUR 6
 \,000 in cash prizes (gross): 1st AI Horizons Prize EUR 1\,500 (overall wi
 nner) plus three sponsor prizes of EUR 1\,500 each (Polo Parma for Parma H
 eritage\, COLSER-Auroradomus for La Cura\, DS Solutions for Sustainability
  and Data Ecology). The top prize can be combined with a sponsor prize\, s
 o one artist can receive up to EUR 3\,000. Prizes are treated as full or p
 artial acquisition of the work. Non-cash: Piazza of Beauty residency in Pa
 rma during the show\, plus Rome New Media Week 2027 and Premio Giovanarte 
 exhibition mentions. Free to enter.\nDuration: Finalist group exhibition i
 n April-May 2027 (11th PARMA 360 Festival)\n\nMore: https://forms.gle/ymoW
 bcjuDyzJY11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://forms.gle/ymoWbcjuDyzJY11P6?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Parma\, Italy. Open to Italian and international artists under 35 
 and students of the Accademie di Belle Arti. Finalists exhibit in Parma in
  April-May 2027.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:american-academy-berlin-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Berlin: Berlin Prize Fellowship 2027-
 28
DESCRIPTION:The American Academy in Berlin is an independent\, nonprofit in
 stitute for advanced study in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\, la
 w\, journalism and public policy\, whose primary mission is to strengthen 
 the cultural and intellectual ties between the United States and Germany. 
 Each year\, after a rigorous selection process\, the Academy awards roughl
 y two dozen semester-long Berlin Prize fellowships to individuals who demo
 nstrate excellence in their fields. DISCIPLINES: applications are welcome 
 across the humanities\, social sciences\, law\, journalism and various are
 as of public policy. The Academy generally encourages projects addressing 
 pressing issues of the day\, specifically naming democracy\, security\, te
 chnology and society (especially AI)\, energy including climate\, and glob
 al order. Dedicated fellowships also support projects in Jewish studies\, 
 German studies\, and public health and biotechnology. Project proposals ne
 ed not focus on Germany\, but candidates should explain how a residency in
  Berlin would enhance their work. NOT ACCEPTED: proposals in mathematics o
 r the natural sciences. NOTE FOR ARTISTS: visual artists and composers are
  invited through separate\, nomination-based competitions\, so there is no
  open application route for them here. ELIGIBILITY: fellowships are restri
 cted to citizens and permanent residents of the United States. Both emergi
 ng and established figures are eligible. PhD holders qualify as emerging s
 cholars with a strong record of peer-reviewed work beyond the dissertation
 \; candidates in non-academic fields such as journalism\, filmmaking and p
 olicy need a significant record of publication or production\; fiction and
  nonfiction writers must have published at least one book with a reputable
  press. WHAT FELLOWS DO: fellows present their work to audiences in and ar
 ound Berlin through lectures\, readings\, public discussions\, performance
 s and film screenings\, and should be willing to engage with relevant Germ
 an institutions\, organizations and the media\; these activities are integ
 ral to the Academy's mission of fostering transatlantic dialogue. APPLICAT
 ION MATERIALS: a project proposal of 1\,500 to 1\,750 words plus a one-pag
 e bibliography\; a curriculum vitae of up to 10 pages\; two writing sample
 s totalling no more than 60 pages\; and three letters of recommendation\, 
 which are due 2 October 2026. DEADLINE: Friday 25 September 2026 at 12:00 
 noon Eastern Time (18:00 Central European Time). TIMELINE: all candidates 
 are notified of the competition outcome by email in late March 2027\; the 
 2027-28 Berlin Prize recipients are announced in May 2027.\n\nOrganisation
 : American Academy in Berlin\nLocation: Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arn
 hold Center. RESTRICTED: fellowships are open only to citizens and permane
 nt residents of the United States.\nAward: Monthly stipend of USD 5\,000\,
  plus roundtrip airfare\, accommodation at or near the Hans Arnhold Center
 \, partial board\, in-house library services and professional networking o
 pportunities. Roughly two dozen fellowships awarded each year. No applicat
 ion fee.\nDuration: One full academic semester (about 4 months). Fall runs
  mid-August to mid-December\; spring runs late January to late May.\n\nMor
 e: https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.americanacademy.de/apply/apply-for-a-fellowship/?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Berlin\, Germany\, at the Hans Arnhold Center. RESTRICTED: fellows
 hips are open only to citizens and permanent residents of the United State
 s.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:we-are-human-festival-call-for-films-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: We Are Human Festival 2026: Call for Films (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:Call for short films (1-10 minutes) involving human/AI hybrid c
 reation\, from the We Are Human Foundation in Paris. Three cash awards: Gr
 and Prix EUR 5\,000\, Best Screenplay EUR 3\,000\, and an Ethics Award EUR
  2\,000. ELIGIBILITY: international\, applicants 18+\; films must have bee
 n completed after 1 June 2025 and involve human/AI hybrid creation\; a man
 datory Ethics Notebook accompanies each submission. No submission fee. Fes
 tival screening at Forum des images\, Paris\, on 24 November 2026. Apply v
 ia FilmFreeway\; deadline 30 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: We Are Human
  Foundation\nLocation: Paris\, France (Forum des images screening 24 Novem
 ber 2026)\nAward: Grand Prix EUR 5\,000\; Best Screenplay EUR 3\,000\; Eth
 ics Award EUR 2\,000. No submission fee.\nDuration: Annual short-film fest
 ival (screening 24 November 2026)\n\nMore: https://wearehuman.foundation/e
 n/call-for-films/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
URL:https://wearehuman.foundation/en/call-for-films/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (Forum des images screening 24 November 2026)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:after-the-palace-resonance-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: AFTER THE PALACE: Resonance 2026 Video Mapping Contest (K
 rakow)
DESCRIPTION:AFTER THE PALACE: Resonance 2026 is an international video mapp
 ing competition and outdoor showcase that asks digital media artists to cr
 eatively reinterpret the dissonant heritage of socialist-era architecture 
 in the context of the history\, cultural identity and memory of Krakow's N
 owa Huta. Artists\, animators\, motion designers\, creative teams and stud
 ios worldwide are invited to create original site-specific projections for
  the courtyard facade of Building Z of the New Administrative Centre\, for
 merly part of the Lenin Steelworks. Organised by the University of the Nat
 ional Education Commission in Krakow as part of the international artistic
  and research project unLoc. TECHNICAL: 2D/3D video mapping with sound\, 1
  to 8 minutes\, MP4 (H.264/AAC) in 4K at 25 fps\, minimum 40 Mbps\, audio 
 48 kHz/16-bit\, built on the dedicated building mapping matrix from the do
 cument package. Generative AI tools are permitted provided their use is fu
 lly disclosed in the application form and the applicant holds rights to th
 e source materials. TIMELINE: submission deadline 30 October 2026\, 23:59 
 CET\; results by 10 November\; outdoor showcase and award ceremony 23 Nove
 mber 2026 in the courtyard at 1 Ujastek St\, Krakow. TO APPLY: submit the 
 online application form with a download link to the work\; the full regula
 tions and mapping matrix are at unloc.art. Contact unloc@uken.krakow.pl.\n
 \nOrganisation: University of the National Education Commission in Krakow 
 (unLoc project)\nLocation: Krakow-Nowa Huta\, Poland. Fully digital submis
 sion from anywhere\; showcase 23 November 2026 on the facade of Building Z
 \, New Administrative Centre (former Lenin Steelworks).\nAward: Cash prize
 s: PLN 10\,000 (~EUR 2\,340) first place\, PLN 6\,000 second\, PLN 3\,000 
 third\; the jury may award additional honorary distinctions or redistribut
 e the pool. Free to enter\, submission is exclusively digital.\n\nMore: ht
 tp://unloc.art/en/news/after-the-palace-en/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:http://unloc.art/en/news/after-the-palace-en/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Krakow-Nowa Huta\, Poland. Fully digital submission from anywhere\
 ; showcase 23 November 2026 on the facade of Building Z\, New Administrati
 ve Centre (former Lenin Steelworks).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:newimages-festival-2027-competitions@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261222
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261223
SUMMARY:Deadline: NewImages Festival 2027: XR\, Fulldome & Virtual Worlds C
 ompetitions (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:NewImages Festival\, the Paris festival for XR and immersive cr
 eation\, opens three competitions for its 2027 edition. XR COMPETITION: wo
 rks completed in 2026 or 2027 in VR\, AR\, mixed reality\, narrative video
  games and hybrid performances\; Grand Prize EUR 6\,000\, Impact Award EUR
  3\,000\; fee EUR 75 Early Bird / EUR 100 Last Call (individual talents EU
 R 45 / EUR 60). FULLDOME COMPETITION: native fulldome (360-degree projecti
 on) works completed after 2023\; Dome Award EUR 3\,000\; same fees as the 
 XR Competition. VIRTUAL WORLDS COMPETITION: social VR platforms\, independ
 ent worlds\, multiplayer art spaces and interactive installations in virtu
 al environments\; Virtual Worlds Award EUR 3\,000\; free to enter. No prem
 iere status required for any competition. Selected works receive festival 
 presentation\, two accreditations and industry visibility. Separate Indust
 ry Days calls (XR Development Market with a EUR 1\,000 Best Project Award\
 , Immersive Art Fair\, XR Partners\, Industry Sessions) run on the same da
 tes. DEADLINES: Early Bird 10 December 2026\, Last Call 22 December 2026.\
 n\nOrganisation: NewImages Festival\nLocation: Paris\, France (festival pr
 esentation\; open internationally)\nAward: XR Competition: Grand Prize EUR
  6\,000 and Impact Award EUR 3\,000. Fulldome Competition: Dome Award EUR 
 3\,000. Virtual Worlds Competition: Virtual Worlds Award EUR 3\,000. Submi
 ssion fees for XR and Fulldome: EUR 75 Early Bird / EUR 100 Last Call (EUR
  45 / EUR 60 for individual talents)\; Virtual Worlds Competition is free 
 to enter. Selected works get festival presentation and two accreditations.
 \nDuration: Festival edition 2027\; submissions open 4 September to 22 Dec
 ember 2026 (Early Bird deadline 10 December 2026).\n\nMore: https://www.ne
 wimages.art/calls-for-projects?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.newimages.art/calls-for-projects?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France (festival presentation\; open internationally)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:dm-award-connecting-worlds-karlsruhe-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261027T174042Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261126
SUMMARY:Deadline: dm-Award connecting worlds 2027: PLAYGROUND (projection m
 apping and public-space media art\, EUR 10\,000 prize plus up to EUR 20\,0
 00 production\, SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE Karlsruhe)
DESCRIPTION:The UNESCO City of Media Arts Office of Karlsruhe's Department 
 of Cultural Affairs awards the dm-Award connecting worlds\, with dm-droger
 ie markt as awarding partner\, ZKM | Center for Art and Media Karlsruhe as
  curatorial partner and KME as organiser of the SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE Light F
 estival. Under the motto PLAYGROUND\, the call seeks projects that connect
  the digital space of the projection mappings on Karlsruhe Palace's facade
  with the analogue space of the Market Square\, playfully activating publi
 c space. FORMAT: every project must have two elements: a projection mappin
 g on the palace facade (2 to 5 minutes) and at least one satellite on the 
 Market Square that also works independently of the projection and is publi
 cly and freely accessible. Examples include interactive projections and ga
 me elements with audience participation\, installations or media artworks 
 relating to the projection\, combinations of performance\, concerts or act
 ions with projection mapping\, sculptural\, 3D or immersive formats\, new 
 technologies\, and collaborations between local and international players.
  The winner is realised in 2027 during the SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE and the exhi
 bition Media art is here\, running four weeks between mid-August and mid-S
 eptember 2027. WHO: artists worldwide\, individually or as a collective. W
 HAT YOU GET: a EUR 10\,000 prize\, up to EUR 20\,000 net production fundin
 g (which must cover all production costs\, including fees\, equipment and 
 the winners' travel)\, plus curatorial and technical support\; technical r
 equirements are set out in the Production Guidelines. APPLICATION: via the
  call page\; questions to cityofmediaarts@kultur.karlsruhe.de. Application
  period 9 October to 25 November 2026\, closing at 13:00 CET.\n\nOrganisat
 ion: Karlsruhe UNESCO City of Media Arts Office (Cultural Office)\, with d
 m-drogerie markt\, ZKM | Center for Art and Media Karlsruhe and KME Karlsr
 uhe Marketing und Event\nLocation: Karlsruhe\, Germany (palace facade and 
 Market Square). Open internationally to individual artists and collectives
 .\nAward: EUR 10\,000 prize plus up to EUR 20\,000 net production funding 
 for the winning project (covering fees\, technical equipment and travel)\,
  with curatorial and technical support from the Cultural Office\, KME and 
 ZKM.\nDuration: Presented for 4 weeks between mid-August and mid-September
  2027 during the SCHLOSSLICHTSPIELE Light Festival and the exhibition Medi
 a art is here.\n\nMore: https://www.cityofmediaarts.de/en/events/apply-now
 -open-call-dm-award-connecting-worlds/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.cityofmediaarts.de/en/events/apply-now-open-call-dm-award-c
 onnecting-worlds/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referra
 l
LOCATION:Karlsruhe\, Germany (palace facade and Market Square). Open intern
 ationally to individual artists and collectives.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
